# qmldir — explicit module manifest for quickshell/modules/ (D-12, closes FM1)
#
# Checking this file in disables Quickshell's directory-scanner synthesis for
# this directory entirely (verified via `quickshell -p ... -v -v`: an
# unmodified tree's `Scanning directory ".../modules"` trace synthesizes
# exactly this file — `module qs.modules` header plus one `Name Version
# File.qml` line per local type). Any .qml type added to this directory that
# is NOT declared below becomes unresolvable to `shell.qml`'s
# `import "modules"` — Phase 12-06 added Colours.qml/Motion.qml here in the
# same commit that created them, per this file's own standing instruction.
# Any FUTURE type added to this directory MUST do the same.
#
# Colours/Motion are marked `singleton` here (12-06, binary-verified) — this
# corrects an earlier assumption (12-RESEARCH.md Pattern 2) that Quickshell's
# `Singleton` root type needs neither `pragma Singleton` nor a qmldir
# `singleton` declaration. Empirically it needs BOTH: without the qmldir
# keyword, bare `Colours.primary`-style access resolves to `undefined`
# forever (the object is never constructed). Colours.qml/Motion.qml each
# carry a matching `pragma Singleton` line for the same reason.
module qs.modules
singleton Colours 1.0 Colours.qml
singleton Motion 1.0 Motion.qml
# One shared scrolling-accent clock (quick task 260824-ns3). Both the edge
# bar strips and the Continuous weld in Bar.qml read it, so a moving gradient
# cannot drift between two surfaces that must join without a seam.
singleton GradientPhase 1.0 GradientPhase.qml
# Prefs (quick-260821-6z1 Task 1, D-02) — the shell-preferences JSON store.
# Registered here, not modules/settings/qmldir, for the same cross-tree
# reason CavaService is registered here rather than modules/dashboard/
# qmldir below: modules/dashboard/Design.qml AND modules/settings/pages/*
# AND shell.qml itself all need to resolve the SAME instance.
singleton Prefs 1.0 Prefs.qml
# WindowInset (quick task 260825-pyf, Task 2) — the live `general:gaps_out`
# read, so a panel aligning to a real window's edge stops hardcoding it.
# Registered here for the same cross-tree reason as Prefs and CavaService:
# modules/bar/, modules/centre/, modules/launcher/ and modules/ itself all
# need the SAME instance, and the whole point is one shared answer rather
# than the four independent copies that had already drifted apart.
singleton WindowInset 1.0 WindowInset.qml
Probe 1.0 Probe.qml
ScreencopyProbe 1.0 ScreencopyProbe.qml
Dashboard 1.0 Dashboard.qml
Overview 1.0 Overview.qml
Bar 1.0 Bar.qml
# CavaService (Phase 21 Plan 01, QMEDIA-02) — the shared cava subprocess
# singleton. Registered here, not modules/dashboard/qmldir, because
# modules/bar/MediaPopout.qml must resolve the SAME instance in a later
# plan; Colours/Motion above are the existing precedent for a singleton
# reached from both dashboard/ and bar/. Carries the singleton keyword
# (12-06's both-required finding — needs pragma Singleton in its own
# source file too, or the type resolves undefined forever with no load
# error).
singleton CavaService 1.0 CavaService.qml
# ThemedToolTip (quick-260821-6z1 fix wave) — the shared themed
# replacement for QQC2's bare attached ToolTip shorthand. Registered
# here, not one leaf directory's own manifest, for the same cross-tree
# reason Prefs/CavaService are: settings/, bar/, dashboard/ and centre/
# call sites all need to resolve the SAME type. Not a singleton — every
# call site owns its own instance, the same shape as Bar/Dashboard/
# Overview above.
ThemedToolTip 1.0 ThemedToolTip.qml
# ThemedScrollBar (quick task 260828-nav) — the shared scroll indicator.
# Registered here rather than in settings/'s own manifest for exactly the
# cross-tree reason ThemedToolTip is: censused 39 files carrying a
# Flickable/ListView/GridView against only 3 carrying a ScrollBar, so this
# type has to resolve from settings/, bar/, dashboard/, centre/, packages/
# and launcher/ alike. Not a singleton — one instance per scrollable
# surface, same posture as ThemedToolTip. Declared in the same commit that
# creates the file, per this manifest's own standing instruction.
ThemedScrollBar 1.0 ThemedScrollBar.qml
# EdgeBar (quick task 260823-9ak, Task 3, R1/R4/D-2) — the always-on top/
# bottom strip. Registered here, a sibling of Bar.qml/Dashboard.qml/
# Overview.qml, deliberately NOT under modules/bar/ — see the file's own
# header for why (GT-4: the colour-role-routing gate scans modules/bar/
# only, and this file needs to read Colours.* directly). Not a singleton —
# shell.qml mounts two ordinary instances (top and bottom), the same
# "one type, N instances" posture as ThemedToolTip above.
EdgeBar 1.0 EdgeBar.qml
